From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:34:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc phone trigger: the underlined words of an
 answerable mail can be chosen

Mode 27 (the phone trigger, original Game.exe 0x456c30) drew the underlined words and kept their hit areas, but
nothing ever chose one: LinkSel stayed 0xFF, so no answer could be sent. The trigger mails are how S;G's mail talks
go on (10:37 type 0x12 makes a mail answerable, the chosen word picks reply slot MailReply + word, type 0x13 turns
the answer into the next mail of the talk in GlobalVars[6825 + slot]); without answers every talk ended at 999 and
MAIN00 could never take the Kurisu route after chapter 10's SG10_04 (it needs mail 334, the end of the talk that
MAIN00 starts with mail 297 before chapter 5) - the game always went to the Mayuri ending.

As in the original: with the mouse or touch the word under the pointer is the chosen one (hit ids 0x30 / 0x44 / 0x58
/ 0x6c are the words 0..3; none when the pointer is elsewhere) and a click or tap takes it in the same frame; with
keys, Up / Down walk over the words of the shown lines (the first press chooses the first word) and scroll past the
ends. The words of the shown lines are the hit areas of the drawn text (S.LinkAreas), the same set the original
gets from its layout pass 0x442520.

Only TYN (SGHD phone). MuMu (Android 15, not a real device), Chinese data, from the start of chapter 5: Kurisu's
talk answered by tapping words 297 -> 301 -> 304 -> 308 -> 316 -> 324 -> 334, mail 334 received and read; the other
talks (425, 518, 550, 554, 614, 429, 437) answered with their first word.

diff --git a/src/games/sghd/phone.cpp b/src/games/sghd/phone.cpp
index 7bb3f874e86e8ec21e5c4c9c91fbd6d432fb67dc..974d4be8bb7f2fb13f3bfdd6a78d81309b83918a 100644
--- a/src/games/sghd/phone.cpp
+++ b/src/games/sghd/phone.cpp
@@ -1111,8 +1111,11 @@ void ModeAfterSend() {
   if (mail != 0xffff) SetMode(S.ReturnMode);
 }
 
-// 0x456c30 mode 27: the phone trigger, choosing an underlined word of the mail. The keyboard walk over the words
-// needs the phone text layout (0x442520) and is not done yet; the words can be picked once the hit areas are in.
+// 0x456c30 mode 27: the phone trigger, choosing an underlined word of the mail (S.LinkSel); the chosen word picks the
+// answer (reply slot MailReply + word). Mouse / touch: the word under the pointer is chosen (none otherwise, the
+// original hit ids 0x30 / 0x44 / 0x58 / 0x6c are the words 0..3) and a click takes it. Keys: Up / Down walk over the
+// words of the shown lines (0x442520 lists them; here the hit areas of the drawn text, S.LinkAreas, are the same
+// set), the first press chooses the first one, past the ends the text scrolls.
 void ModePhoneTrigger() {
   const int mail = SW(0x6a5c);
   if (Cancel()) {
@@ -1123,6 +1126,12 @@ void ModePhoneTrigger() {
   S.ScrollHover = 0;
   S.Hover = 0;
   MailScroll(0, 0x6a78, 0x6a74);
+  if (MouseMode()) {
+    S.LinkSel = 0xff;
+    for (uint32_t word = 0; word < 4; word++)
+      if (Hit(48 + 20 * word, 1)) S.Hover = 1, S.LinkSel = word;
+    if (Hit(0, 8)) ClickDecide();
+  }
   if (Decide()) {
     if (S.Mails[mail][MailAttach] == 999) {
       if (!GetFlag(0xa29) || !GetFlag(0xa35) || mail != SW(0x6aa0) || S.Mails[mail][MailReply] == 999 ||
@@ -1137,7 +1146,27 @@ void ModePhoneTrigger() {
     SetMode(0x1c);
     return;
   }
-  if (!MouseMode()) MailScrollKeys(0x6a78, 0x6a74);
+  if (MouseMode()) return;
+  const bool up = Up(), down = Down();
+  if (up == down) return;
+  std::vector<uint32_t> shown;  // the words of the shown lines, in order
+  for (const auto& a : S.LinkAreas)
+    if (std::find(shown.begin(), shown.end(), (uint32_t)a.Word) == shown.end()) shown.push_back((uint32_t)a.Word);
+  const auto at = std::find(shown.begin(), shown.end(), S.LinkSel);
+  if (at == shown.end()) {
+    if (!shown.empty()) {
+      S.LinkSel = shown.front();
+      return;
+    }
+  } else if (up && at != shown.begin()) {
+    S.LinkSel = *(at - 1);
+    return;
+  } else if (down && at + 1 != shown.end()) {
+    S.LinkSel = *(at + 1);
+    return;
+  }
+  if (up && SW(0x6a74) != 0) SW(0x6a74)--;
+  if (down && (uint32_t)SW(0x6a78) > 12 && (uint32_t)SW(0x6a74) < (uint32_t)SW(0x6a78) - 12) SW(0x6a74)++;
 }
 
 // 0x457310 mode 28: answer with the chosen word or open the attachment
